              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কয়লা (kôylā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from kokila, \"lighted coal, charcoal\" (CDIAL 3484). CDIAL reports the view that Sanskrit took the word from Munda, comparing Santali kuila, \"black\"."
